{
  "format": "lcir.lesson",
  "formatVersion": 3,
  "id": "basic-gates",
  "title": "The basic gates",
  "workbench": "circuit",
  "board": "basic-gates",
  "steps": [
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "headline": "Two inputs, seven gates",
      "prose": "One pair of inputs, **A** and **B**, feeds every gate on this board. Each gate drives its own LED, so you can read the truth table straight off the lamps.",
      "actions": [
        { "kind": "power", "on": true },
        { "kind": "highlight", "components": ["a", "b"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "headline": "Three groups",
      "prose": "**AND**, **OR** and **XOR** are the true-output gates. **NAND**, **NOR** and **XNOR** are the same three with an inverter on the output. The **NOT** gate is the odd one out: it takes **A** only.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "kind": "highlight",
          "components": ["g_and", "g_or", "g_xor", "g_nand", "nor27", "xnor24", "g_not"]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "predict",
      "prose": "Set **A** = 1 and **B** = 1. Which LEDs light?",
      "choices": [
        { "text": "AND, OR, NAND" },
        { "text": "AND, OR, XNOR", "right": true },
        { "text": "OR, XOR, NAND" },
        { "text": "NOT A, NOR, XNOR" }
      ],
      "answer": "AND is 1 only when both inputs are 1. OR is 1 when at least one is. XOR is 1 only when the inputs differ, so it is off here, and its inverse **XNOR** is on. NAND and NOR are off, and **NOT A** is off because A = 1.",
      "actions": [
        { "kind": "row", "index": 3, "set": [1, 1], "when": "reveal" },
        {
          "kind": "highlight",
          "components": ["l_and", "l_or", "l_xor", "l_nand", "l_not", "led28", "led29"]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "headline": "A = 0, B = 1",
      "prose": "Now **A** = 0 and **B** = 1. AND goes dark, but OR and XOR stay lit. **NOT A** lights because it only looks at **A**.",
      "actions": [
        { "kind": "row", "index": 1, "set": [0, 1], "when": "open" },
        { "kind": "highlight", "components": ["l_and", "l_or", "l_xor", "l_not"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "predict",
      "prose": "Set both inputs to 0. Which LEDs light?",
      "choices": [
        { "text": "None of them" },
        { "text": "NOT A, NAND, NOR, XNOR", "right": true },
        { "text": "NOT A, AND, OR" }
      ],
      "answer": "With both inputs 0, AND, OR and XOR are all 0, so their inverted partners **NAND**, **NOR** and **XNOR** are all 1. **NOT A** is 1 because A = 0.",
      "actions": [
        { "kind": "row", "index": 0, "set": [0, 0], "when": "reveal" },
        { "kind": "highlight", "components": ["l_nand", "led28", "led29", "l_not"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "headline": "Each inverted gate is its partner's complement",
      "prose": "Compare the pairs down all four input rows. **NAND** is always the opposite of **AND**, **NOR** the opposite of **OR**, and **XNOR** the opposite of **XOR**. Only **XOR** and **XNOR** care whether the inputs are equal.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "kind": "highlight",
          "components": ["l_and", "l_nand", "l_or", "led28", "l_xor", "led29"]
        },
        { "kind": "tab", "tab": "sequence" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "predict",
      "prose": "The board shows **A** = 0, **B** = 1. Swap the inputs to **A** = 1, **B** = 0. Which LEDs change?",
      "choices": [
        { "text": "Only NOT A", "right": true },
        { "text": "AND and OR" },
        { "text": "Every LED" }
      ],
      "answer": "AND, OR, XOR and their inverses give the same result when you swap A and B, so none of them change. Only **NOT A** changes, from 1 to 0, because it reads **A** alone.",
      "actions": [
        { "kind": "row", "index": 1, "set": [0, 1], "when": "open" },
        { "kind": "row", "index": 2, "set": [1, 0], "when": "reveal" },
        { "kind": "highlight", "components": ["l_not"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "headline": "Walk the whole table",
      "prose": "Step through all four rows with `]` and `[`. Say each LED pattern aloud before the next row.",
      "actions": [{ "kind": "tab", "tab": "sequence" }]
    }
  ]
}
